%% Pending context-action request state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle

  state "Idle / no pending context tap" as Idle
  note right of Idle
    No pending tap candidate exists.
    There is no document mutation, selection change,
    preview state, repaint request, or action event.
  end note

  Idle --> Disposed: "runtime.dispose()"
  Idle --> FirstTapGate: "finite tap or click admitted"
  Idle --> DirectDoubleTapGate: "host-recognized handleDoubleTap with finite position"
  Idle --> Idle: "invalid, stale, drag, active pointer conflict, or wrong mode / ignore"

  state "Direct double-tap gate" as DirectDoubleTapGate
  note right of DirectDoubleTapGate
    Direct handleDoubleTap is a host-recognized
    input event. It does not require pending
    first-tap history, but clears stale pending
    context tap history through PointerToolCleanupCoordinator
    before resolving the current target.
  end note

  DirectDoubleTapGate --> DirectTopTarget: "resolve timestamp and query current content hit candidates"

  state "Direct current target resolution" as DirectTopTarget
  note right of DirectTopTarget
    Direct double-tap resolves the current
    context-action target at the supplied position:
    top visible content element or empty canvas.
  end note

  DirectTopTarget --> EmitContentRequest: "current content target"
  DirectTopTarget --> EmitEmptyCanvasRequest: "current empty-canvas target"

  state "First tap gate" as FirstTapGate
  note right of FirstTapGate
    First tap detection is gesture tracking only.
    It reads current target data and may remember
    a content-element or empty-canvas candidate.
  end note

  FirstTapGate --> TopTargetFirst: "query committed content hit candidates"
  FirstTapGate --> Idle: "non-finite world position or tapSlop exceeded / no request"

  state "First target resolution" as TopTargetFirst
  note right of TopTargetFirst
    Context-action targeting uses visible content,
    finite invertible transforms, exact geometry,
    and topmost content paint order.
    element.isSelectable is not a gate.
    Background-only coverage resolves as empty canvas.
  end note

  TopTargetFirst --> PendingContentTarget: "top content target / store id, generation, elementRevision, family, positions, timestamp, epoch"
  TopTargetFirst --> PendingEmptyCanvas: "no qualifying content target / store empty-canvas candidate"

  state "Pending content target" as PendingContentTarget
  note right of PendingContentTarget
    Pending state is input history only:
    element id, generation, elementRevision, family,
    view/world positions, timestamp, and controllerEpoch.
    It is not CanvasPreviewState and not Store state.
  end note

  state "Pending empty-canvas target" as PendingEmptyCanvas
  note right of PendingEmptyCanvas
    Empty-canvas pending state carries positions,
    timestamp, and controllerEpoch only.
    It has no element snapshot.
  end note

  PendingContentTarget --> SecondTapGate: "second tap"
  PendingEmptyCanvas --> SecondTapGate: "second tap"
  PendingContentTarget --> DirectDoubleTapGate: "host-recognized finite handleDoubleTap / clear pending context tap"
  PendingEmptyCanvas --> DirectDoubleTapGate: "host-recognized finite handleDoubleTap / clear pending context tap"
  PendingContentTarget --> CleanupOnly: "delay exceeded, slop exceeded, invalid sample, mode mismatch, controllerEpoch mismatch, mode change, or interactive=false"
  PendingEmptyCanvas --> CleanupOnly: "delay exceeded, slop exceeded, invalid sample, mode mismatch, controllerEpoch mismatch, mode change, or interactive=false"
  PendingContentTarget --> CleanupOnly: "loadDocument success after install"
  PendingEmptyCanvas --> CleanupOnly: "loadDocument success after install"
  PendingContentTarget --> PendingContentTarget: "loadDocument validation/materialization failure before install / preserve tap"
  PendingEmptyCanvas --> PendingEmptyCanvas: "loadDocument validation/materialization failure before install / preserve tap"
  PendingContentTarget --> DisposeCleanup: "runtime.dispose()"
  PendingEmptyCanvas --> DisposeCleanup: "runtime.dispose()"

  state "Second tap gate" as SecondTapGate
  note right of SecondTapGate
    The second tap must match the same target class
    and be revalidated against the current document
    and current epoch.
  end note

  SecondTapGate --> CleanupOnly: "non-finite world position, tapSlop exceeded, doubleTapSlop exceeded, or delay exceeded"
  SecondTapGate --> TopTargetSecond: "query current committed content hit candidates"

  state "Second target resolution" as TopTargetSecond
  note right of TopTargetSecond
    A content target must still be the same topmost
    visible content element. An empty-canvas target
    must still have no qualifying content target.
  end note

  TopTargetSecond --> CandidateMatch: "same target class"
  TopTargetSecond --> CleanupOnly: "target class changed / clear pending only"

  state "Candidate match gate" as CandidateMatch
  note right of CandidateMatch
    Content targets match by current element id,
    generation, elementRevision, family,
    controllerEpoch, visibility, and top-hit status.
    Empty-canvas targets match by still having no
    qualifying content target.
  end note

  CandidateMatch --> CleanupOnly: "different content target, stale generation, stale elementRevision, hidden, family mismatch, epoch mismatch, or new content target"
  CandidateMatch --> EmitContentRequest: "same current content target"
  CandidateMatch --> EmitEmptyCanvasRequest: "still empty canvas"

  state "Issue content context request" as EmitContentRequest
  note right of EmitContentRequest
    InteractionEngine issues CanvasInteractionRequestId
    through InteractionRequestRegistry, then emits
    CanvasContextActionRequested with doubleTap trigger,
    content target kind, immutable CanvasElement snapshot,
    boundsWorld, positions, timestamp, controllerEpoch,
    and documentRevision. documentRevision is observation-only.
  end note

  state "Issue empty-canvas context request" as EmitEmptyCanvasRequest
  note right of EmitEmptyCanvasRequest
    InteractionEngine issues CanvasInteractionRequestId
    through InteractionRequestRegistry, then emits
    CanvasContextActionRequested with doubleTap trigger,
    empty-canvas target kind, positions, timestamp,
    controllerEpoch, and documentRevision.
  end note

  EmitContentRequest --> IssuedRequestLive: "request delivered / clear pending tap and keep request id live"
  EmitEmptyCanvasRequest --> IssuedRequestLive: "request delivered / clear pending tap and keep request id live"

  state "Issued request remains live" as IssuedRequestLive
  note right of IssuedRequestLive
    The application owns context menus, editor overlays,
    IME, focus, accessibility, hide/show policy, and any
    later commitTextEdit text commit flow.
    Pending tap history is already cleared.
    The registry is not an app UI session and not CanvasPreviewState.
  end note

  IssuedRequestLive --> RetiredRequest: "commitTextEdit accepted no-op or changed text content request / retire request"
  IssuedRequestLive --> RetiredRequest: "commitTextEdit rejected stale, empty-canvas, non-text, missing, retired, or family-mismatched request"
  IssuedRequestLive --> RetiredRequest: "loadDocument success / controllerEpoch makes request stale"
  IssuedRequestLive --> Disposed: "runtime.dispose() / later commitTextEdit throws StateError"

  state "Retired or stale request id" as RetiredRequest
  note right of RetiredRequest
    Retired and epoch-stale request ids cannot commit.
    Text commit acceptance requires a current,
    unretired text content target request.
    documentRevision is not a stale guard.
  end note

  RetiredRequest --> Idle: "request lifecycle closed"

  state "Cleanup only" as CleanupOnly
  note left of CleanupOnly
    Cleanup creates a typed request for the
    PointerToolCleanupCoordinator to clear pending tap history only.
    It publishes no context request, action event,
    document revision, selection change, preview update,
    spatial update, projection eviction, or repaint.
  end note

  CleanupOnly --> CleanupCoordinator: "typed cleanup request"
  DisposeCleanup --> CleanupCoordinator: "typed cleanup request before stream close"
  CleanupCoordinator --> Idle: "pending context target cleared after ordinary cleanup"
  CleanupCoordinator --> Disposed: "pending context target cleared before runtime streams close"
  Disposed --> [*]
